msgctxt "Words"
msgid ""
"Your vault server makes a one-time invite and this phone shows it as a QR "
"code, for an hour. The other device still needs your master password and "
"Secret Key."
msgstr ""

#: ui/app.slint:252
msgctxt "Words"
msgid ""
"Type it once to open the key. The vault keeps the key without it: the vault "
"itself protects it, and the copy you take out works without a passphrase."
msgstr ""

#: ui/app.slint:253
msgctxt "Words"
msgid ""
"A newer version of this app is out. Android asks you before it installs it, "
"and installs it only if it is signed like the app you have. Later, it waits "
"in Settings, Updates."
msgstr ""

#: ui/app.slint:254
msgctxt "Words"
msgid ""
"Another device renewed the vault key and printed a new kit. Type the Secret "
"Key from that kit, and your master password: this phone then keeps the new "
"key and syncs again. Unlock with the phone turns off until you turn it on "
"again."
msgstr ""

#: ui/app.slint:255
msgctxt "Words"
msgid ""
"After 10 failed tries in a row to unlock this vault here, this phone deletes "
"its copy of the vault file, its unlock with the phone and the key in the "
"phone's secure hardware behind it, the Secret Key kept on this phone, and "
"this phone's sync key for the vault. Nothing is sent to your sync server: "
"its copies stay, and your other devices keep the vault. To use it here "
"again, join it again with an invite from another device."
msgstr ""

